  },
  {
    "id": "session-12-scyldgar-keep_summary",
    "type": "text",
    "props": {
      "content": "After the assassination attempt on Mollywop, the Souls of Destiny rode north from Adsuren determined to track the fleeing assassin, Esylla’s uncle Ifryn, and uncover whatever larger threat still moved in the shadows. They followed the blood trail through the woods to a ruined keep once held by the cutthroat Scyldgar family, a place that stirred both Lila’s visions and Therric’s recurring dreams of a great cat protecting a younger Areana Duskwhisper. Inside they faced rising undead skeletons that Escanor banished in a single radiant command, then battled living gargoyles that took flight from the rooftop statues, with Zephyra’s rage, Lila’s magic, and Kenton’s whip ending the fight. The session closed as Zephyra discovered a red, smoky horse figure still waiting in the stables and Kenton and Lila found a golden stick gleaming inside an untouched chest, the keep holding both old secrets and the continuing trail of their quarry.",
      "col": "1",
      "row": "3",
      "colSpan": "1",
      "rowSpan": "1"
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "session-11-it-s-market-day_title",
    "type": "header",
    "props": {
      "title": "Session 11 - It’s Market Day",
      "color": "gold",
      "size": "md",
      "audioLinks": "[\n  {\n    \"label\": \"11 - It's Market Day.mp3\",\n    \"url\": \"/media/session-audio/souls-of-destiny/session-11-1T9hdmVXOtmeZi0Zo6ezzaanKXF8HEK-y.mp3\",\n    \"sourceFileId\": \"1T9hdmVXOtmeZi0Zo6ezzaanKXF8HEK-y\",\n    \"sourceFileName\": \"11 - It's Market Day.mp3\",\n    \"sourceUrl\": \"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1T9hdmVXOtmeZi0Zo6ezzaanKXF8HEK-y/view?usp=sharing\"\n  }\n]",
      "col": "1",
      "row": "4",
      "colSpan": "1",
      "rowSpan": "1"
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "session-11-it-s-market-day_summary",
    "type": "text",
    "props": {
      "content": "The party returned to the lively Market Day in Adsuren ready to unwind, sell their goods, shop for essentials, and stay sharp for any signs of the mysterious plan. They split up and enjoyed Market Day, procuring gifts for one another.  Market Day wasn’t all fun, as they had to deal with some Tirncall thugs attempting a robbery at the silk shop. Hours later the evening festivities turned deadly when an assassin plunged a poisoned great sword through Mollywop’s back during her spectacular dragon-illusion finale, sparking a chaotic combat with nets, restraints, and his gang of thugs where the party fought hard amid civilian deaths.  The party prevailed, but the main assassin fled as Mollywop died from the deadly poison.  In a vengeful rage, the party pursued the assassin.",
      "col": "1",
      "row": "5",
      "colSpan": "1",
      "rowSpan": "1"
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "session-10-fools-gold_title",
    "type": "header",
    "props": {
      "title": "Session 10 - Fools Gold",
      "color": "gold",
      "size": "md",
      "audioLinks": "[\n  {\n    \"label\": \"10 - Fools Gold.mp3\",\n    \"url\": \"/media/session-audio/souls-of-destiny/session-10-1VCOaCMtvfosNDNmiARjH92fng2mwN1Gx.mp3\",\n    \"sourceFileId\": \"1VCOaCMtvfosNDNmiARjH92fng2mwN1Gx\",\n    \"sourceFileName\": \"10 - Fools Gold.mp3\",\n    \"sourceUrl\": \"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1VCOaCMtvfosNDNmiARjH92fng2mwN1Gx/view?usp=sharing\"\n  }\n]",
      "col": "1",
      "row": "6",
      "colSpan": "1",
      "rowSpan": "1"
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "session-10-fools-gold_summary",
    "type": "text",
    "props": {
      "content": "The Souls of Destiny sought to confront the threat that had triggered Mollywop's alarm and discover its nature. Lila, who had stayed behind, arrived via magic and recognized the infected golden dragon Cabristrasz from a vivid vision of its life growing from a starry cave through forests and swamps until it rested in a swamp tree overtaken by vines and fungi. The party fought the majestic yet corrupted beast, finally felling the dragon. Mollywop soon secured the body with telekinesis, shared that she had known the young dragon years ago before its infection in the Sapcutts' swamp, and promised aid from a cleric while messaging a larger gold dragon on Inverland as the party turned back to Market Day with plans to head toward Caldwynn.",
      "col": "1",
      "row": "7",
      "colSpan": "1",
      "rowSpan": "1"
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "session-9-that-s-a-good-looking-dwarf_title",
    "type": "header",
    "props": {
      "title": "Session 9 - That's a Good Looking Dwarf",
      "color": "gold",
      "size": "md",
      "audioLinks": "[\n  {\n    \"label\": \"09 - Thats a Good Looking Dwarf.mp3\",\n    \"url\": \"/media/session-audio/souls-of-destiny/session-9-1ZMcCpi2jpWhmCEAdBAElmSfd6wyMspzK.mp3\",\n    \"sourceFileId\": \"1ZMcCpi2jpWhmCEAdBAElmSfd6wyMspzK\",\n    \"sourceFileName\": \"09 - Thats a Good Looking Dwarf.mp3\",\n    \"sourceUrl\": \"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1ZMcCpi2jpWhmCEAdBAElmSfd6wyMspzK/view?usp=sharing\"\n  }\n]",
      "col": "1",
      "row": "8",
      "colSpan": "1",
      "rowSpan": "1"
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "session-9-that-s-a-good-looking-dwarf_summary",
    "type": "text",
    "props": {
      "content": "The party decided to check reports of a raging bulas near the mines before aiding Mollywop with Market Day preparations. Therric a dream of prowling beside a white-leaved woman to a keep with three-horn tapestries and Escanor a harrowing vision of his own shadow self denying redemption before a flaming combat that ended with the entity turning to ash.  The thick-skinned bulas charged in the next morning and was slain. Back in town they traded the pelt for magic boots.  Then on Market Day, Mollywop's alarm sent them to a fisherman's hut where a large creature erupted from the river.",
      "col": "1",
      "row": "9",
      "colSpan": "1",
      "rowSpan": "1"
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "session-8-devil-spawn_title",
    "type": "header",
    "props": {
      "title": "Session 8 - Devil Spawn",
      "color": "gold",
      "size": "md",
      "audioLinks": "[\n  {\n    \"label\": \"08 - Devil Spawn.mp3\",\n    \"url\": \"/media/session-audio/souls-of-destiny/session-8-1RZWWc0pMrk6F6T7CBK86TvoIvXJ64RXX.mp3\",\n    \"sourceFileId\": \"1RZWWc0pMrk6F6T7CBK86TvoIvXJ64RXX\",\n    \"sourceFileName\": \"08 - Devil Spawn.mp3\",\n    \"sourceUrl\": \"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1RZWWc0pMrk6F6T7CBK86TvoIvXJ64RXX/view?usp=sharing\"\n  }\n]",
      "col": "1",
      "row": "10",
      "colSpan": "1",
      "rowSpan": "1"
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "session-8-devil-spawn_summary",
    "type": "text",
    "props": {
      "content": "The party plunged into the hidden cellar beneath the Adsuren Center determined to root out the Cult of the Immured and shatter their blood rituals before more townsfolk fell victim. They carved through chanting cultists in a gore-slicked chamber only to unmask the respected Intendant Eyovar Dunajor as the fiendish summoner Karranok. The interrupted rite summoned the succubus Aeolenne who promptly declared Zephyra her daughter sparking a chaotic battle. Though the demoness escaped, the party dismantled the cult, delivered justice to its traitor and emerged victorious with treasures, revelations and fresh resolve to press on into the mines..",
      "col": "1",
      "row": "11",
      "colSpan": "1",
      "rowSpan": "1"
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "session-7-a-solid-plan_title",
    "type": "header",
    "props": {
      "title": "Session 7 - A Solid Plan",
      "color": "gold",
      "size": "md",
      "audioLinks": "[\n  {\n    \"label\": \"07 - A Solid Plan.mp3\",\n    \"url\": \"/media/session-audio/souls-of-destiny/session-7-1_yWZston6bYsRlP6lSrO59-HLoMK9Caj.mp3\",\n    \"sourceFileId\": \"1_yWZston6bYsRlP6lSrO59-HLoMK9Caj\",\n    \"sourceFileName\": \"07 - A Solid Plan.mp3\",\n    \"sourceUrl\": \"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1_yWZston6bYsRlP6lSrO59-HLoMK9Caj/view?usp=sharing\"\n  }\n]",
      "col": "1",
      "row": "12",
      "colSpan": "1",
      "rowSpan": "1"
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "session-7-a-solid-plan_summary",
    "type": "text",
    "props": {
      "content": "The party aimed to raid the cellar beneath Adsuren Center, their strongest lead on the cult, while deflecting blame for the missing town taxes. Esylla found Mollywop oddly exhausted.  They planted stolen gold in Ganon’s boarding house to get the guards off their trail.  They descended into the cellar that night, proving it to be the hideout they were hoping to find. They found cultists and evidence of their rituals using hearts and black salt. Descending deeper and disposing of more cultists, the session ended at a set of double doors deep beneath Adsuren.",
      "col": "1",
      "row": "13",
      "colSpan": "1",
      "rowSpan": "1"
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "session-6-who-took-it_title",
    "type": "header",
    "props": {
      "title": "Session 6 - Who Took It?",
      "color": "gold",
      "size": "md",
      "audioLinks": "[\n  {\n    \"label\": \"06 - Who Took It.mp3\",\n    \"url\": \"/media/session-audio/souls-of-destiny/session-6-1bZuRvD9TeZ1z22PHqzqUTquIXYR8FndI.mp3\",\n    \"sourceFileId\": \"1bZuRvD9TeZ1z22PHqzqUTquIXYR8FndI\",\n    \"sourceFileName\": \"06 - Who Took It.mp3\",\n    \"sourceUrl\": \"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1bZuRvD9TeZ1z22PHqzqUTquIXYR8FndI/view?usp=sharing\"\n  }\n]",
      "col": "1",
      "row": "14",
      "colSpan": "1",
      "rowSpan": "1"
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "session-6-who-took-it_summary",
    "type": "text",
    "props": {
      "content": "The party set out from Mollywop’s tower determined to uncover the location of the rituals plaguing Adsuren and this Summoner Karranock.  The heart-harvesting rites were taking place somewhere deeper in town. The day unfolded with tavern intrigue, dockside questioning, and a tense search of Ganon’s rented room that revealed twitching rat heads and precise instructions for creating black salt from sentient hearts. Kenton added his own complications by quietly lifting tax pouches from the Adsuren Center, an act that quickly turned the town’s Market Day preparations into a flurry of guarded suspicion. By session’s end the Souls of Destiny found themselves chasing a shadowy cult while trying not to trip over the fresh chaos one of their own had sown.",
      "col": "1",
      "row": "15",
      "colSpan": "1",
      "rowSpan": "1"
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "session-5-thugs-and-cultists_title",
    "type": "header",
    "props": {
      "title": "Session 5 - Thugs & Cultists",
      "color": "gold",
      "size": "md",
      "audioLinks": "[\n  {\n    \"label\": \"05 - Thugs and Cultists.mp3\",\n    \"url\": \"/media/session-audio/souls-of-destiny/session-5-1NpK-tNkffM9QkwSv96Jn6kBRE3aSQ69q.mp3\",\n    \"sourceFileId\": \"1NpK-tNkffM9QkwSv96Jn6kBRE3aSQ69q\",\n    \"sourceFileName\": \"05 - Thugs and Cultists.mp3\",\n    \"sourceUrl\": \"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1NpK-tNkffM9QkwSv96Jn6kBRE3aSQ69q/view?usp=sharing\"\n  }\n]",
      "col": "1",
      "row": "16",
      "colSpan": "1",
      "rowSpan": "1"
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "session-5-thugs-and-cultists_summary",
    "type": "text",
    "props": {
      "content": "The party set out to track the shadowy cult responsible for poisoning Adsuren’s well. Most of the group interrogated the local tanner and battled his cultist apprentice Ganon.  However, Kenton was ambushed in an alley by thugs led by Sir Rodolf Norran from Gibuldon. Rodolf left behind a healing potion marked “Ryvennra” after Kenton fell. The party then consulted Mollywop the Magnificent, who identified the cult’s lesser fiendish amulet and unholy black salt, and used Speak with Dead to learn that Summoner Karranock leads the group and their outdoor rituals occur somewhere deeper in Adsuren. Now aware that an imp may have alerted the cult, the heroes must carefully flush out their hidden enemies without alarming the village, while also bracing for Rodolf’s next move.",
      "col": "1",
      "row": "17",
      "colSpan": "1",
      "rowSpan": "1"
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "session-4-putrid_title",
    "type": "header",
    "props": {
      "title": "Session 4 - Putrid",
      "color": "gold",
      "size": "md",
      "audioLinks": "[\n  {\n    \"label\": \"04 - Putrid.mp3\",\n    \"url\": \"/media/session-audio/souls-of-destiny/session-4-1QrNtaYGo2uDTV3KSxas1G0v-GYY63QXl.mp3\",\n    \"sourceFileId\": \"1QrNtaYGo2uDTV3KSxas1G0v-GYY63QXl\",\n    \"sourceFileName\": \"04 - Putrid.mp3\",\n    \"sourceUrl\": \"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1QrNtaYGo2uDTV3KSxas1G0v-GYY63QXl/view?usp=sharing\"\n  }\n]",
      "col": "1",
      "row": "18",
      "colSpan": "1",
      "rowSpan": "1"
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "session-4-putrid_summary",
    "type": "text",
    "props": {
      "content": "Returning to Adsuren the group sought answers about the growing corruption tied to stolen hearts and the ritual they had uncovered in the swamp. After consulting Mollywop, they learned the heart was human, bound by necromancy and fiendish magic, and likely created by a hidden group operating within the town itself. Investigating the graveyard, they confirmed their fears when an unearthed body missing its heart rose as an undead attacker. After destroying it, they were working with the early signs of a cult working in secret among Adsuren’s people.  Spreading out for more information led to an untimely attack upon Kenton, with the party unaware.",
      "col": "1",
      "row": "19",
      "colSpan": "1",
      "rowSpan": "1"
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "session-3-fungipheliac-using-kinfolk_title",
    "type": "header",
    "props": {
      "title": "Session 3 - Fungipheliac Using Kinfolk",
      "color": "gold",
      "size": "md",
      "audioLinks": "[\n  {\n    \"label\": \"03 - Fungapheliac Using Kinfolk.mp3\",\n    \"url\": \"/media/session-audio/souls-of-destiny/session-3-1Ulp2O0rIsSBTTAnCmpv-2Yo5tpoLH0es.mp3\",\n    \"sourceFileId\": \"1Ulp2O0rIsSBTTAnCmpv-2Yo5tpoLH0es\",\n    \"sourceFileName\": \"03 - Fungapheliac Using Kinfolk.mp3\",\n    \"sourceUrl\": \"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1Ulp2O0rIsSBTTAnCmpv-2Yo5tpoLH0es/view?usp=sharing\"\n  }\n]",
      "col": "1",
      "row": "20",
      "colSpan": "1",
      "rowSpan": "1"
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "session-3-fungipheliac-using-kinfolk_summary",
    "type": "text",
    "props": {
      "content": "The party sought to uncover what had happened to the missing Sapcutt family after being betrayed and trapped beneath their home. Fighting through fungal undead and deadly traps, they discovered the house itself was sustained by a sentient corruption born from something pulled out of the swamp. By rescuing Lobella and learning the grim bargain her mother had made, the party chose to save the living rather than destroy everything in their path. They escaped into the night with the surviving Sapcutts, knowing the true source of the corruption still lurked somewhere beyond the house.",
      "col": "1",
      "row": "21",
      "colSpan": "1",
      "rowSpan": "1"
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "session-2-mollywop-to-sapcutt_title",
    "type": "header",
    "props": {
      "title": "Session 2 - Mollywop to Sapcutt",
      "color": "gold",
      "size": "md",
      "audioLinks": "[\n  {\n    \"label\": \"02 - Mollywop to Sapcutt.mp3\",\n    \"url\": \"/media/session-audio/souls-of-destiny/session-2-1z2iws29s3qYPisVZ2tj0b-WRHjd3ThdF.mp3\",\n    \"sourceFileId\": \"1z2iws29s3qYPisVZ2tj0b-WRHjd3ThdF\",\n    \"sourceFileName\": \"02 - Mollywop to Sapcutt.mp3\",\n    \"sourceUrl\": \"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1z2iws29s3qYPisVZ2tj0b-WRHjd3ThdF/view?usp=sharing\"\n  }\n]",
      "col": "1",
      "row": "22",
      "colSpan": "1",
      "rowSpan": "1"
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "session-2-mollywop-to-sapcutt_summary",
    "type": "text",
    "props": {
      "content": "After saving Adsuren’s well, the party sought to understand the darker magic behind the corruption and welcomed a new companion, Lila, into their ranks. They destroyed the tainted heart under holy blessing and set out to consult Mollywop the Magnificent for deeper insight. In exchange for her help, they agreed to investigate the disappearance of the Sapcutt family and traveled into the swampy lowlands beyond the river. What began as a warm welcome at the Sapcutt ranch ended in betrayal, as the party was drugged during dinner and dropped through a hidden pit beneath the house.",
      "col": "1",
      "row": "23",
      "colSpan": "1",
      "rowSpan": "1"
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "session-1-we-meet_title",
    "type": "header",
    "props": {
      "title": "Session 1 - We Meet",
      "color": "gold",
      "size": "md",
      "audioLinks": "[\n  {\n    \"label\": \"01 - We Meet.mp3\",\n    \"url\": \"/media/session-audio/souls-of-destiny/session-1-1XctceACyRxJYDtrH9AP-j5JPaDDzLsDq.mp3\",\n    \"sourceFileId\": \"1XctceACyRxJYDtrH9AP-j5JPaDDzLsDq\",\n    \"sourceFileName\": \"01 - We Meet.mp3\",\n    \"sourceUrl\": \"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1XctceACyRxJYDtrH9AP-j5JPaDDzLsDq/view?usp=sharing\"\n  }\n]",
      "col": "1",
      "row": "24",
      "colSpan": "1",
      "rowSpan": "1"
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "session-1-we-meet_summary",
    "type": "text",
    "props": {
      "content": "In their first meeting in Adsuren, the newly formed party was drawn together by a sudden crisis when a villager collapsed after drinking from the town well. What began as a chance encounter quickly became a shared purpose as they set out to discover the source of the poisoning threatening the village. Their investigation led them beneath the settlement, where they fought through restless undead and uncovered a corrupted underground stream. By destroying the unnatural growth tainting the water and recovering its disturbing remnants, the party saved the well and prevented further harm, while realizing their brief alliance had become something more permanent.",
      "col": "1",
      "row": "25",
      "colSpan": "1",
      "rowSpan": "1"
    }
  }
]"
    }
  }
]
